# Template for Config/secrets.properties, which is NOT committed.
#
# Copy this file to secrets.properties in the same folder and put your own Gmail
# app password in it. That is all a local run needs for the mailbox to work:
#
#   - the six digit registration code is read over IMAP instead of being typed
#   - the report for the run is emailed out over SMTP when the suite finishes
#
# Both use this one value, so if one works the other will too.
#
# Where to get it: https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords - a Google account
# password will not work here, it has to be an app password. Google shows it in
# four groups of four; paste it either way, the spaces are ignored.
#
# IMAP also has to be switched on for the mailbox, under
# Gmail Settings > Forwarding and POP/IMAP > Enable IMAP.
#
# This file is only one of three places the password is looked for, in order:
#
#   1. -Dumpay.mail.password=... on the command line   (a one-off run, or CI)
#   2. the UMPAY_MAIL_PASSWORD environment variable
#   3. this file
#
# An environment variable still wins over this file, so setting one for CI does
# not clash with having this on a developer machine.

mail.password=xxxx xxxx xxxx xxxx
